[2026-04-02 16:35:47.358] [default] [INFO] [proxy.go:89] 开始发送请求 &{POST https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1/chat/completions HTTP/1.1 1 1 map[Authorization:[Bearer sk-da6d7a7da1914f6581d4825d7b790389] Content-Type:[application/json]] {{"model":"qwen3.5-flash","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are an intent classification module in an AI agent system.\n\nYour task is to classify the user's request into exactly ONE of the following categories:\nMUST start with { and end with } and follow the JSON format strictly,or it will be considered as an error.\n\nIF the request is ambiguous, set \"requires_clarification\" to true.\n\n1. PLAN\n- The request requires multi-step reasoning, task decomposition, or long-term execution.\n- The task cannot be completed in a single tool call.\n- The user intent implies a workflow, pipeline, or goal-oriented process.\n- Examples: \"Build a trading bot\", \"Help me plan a trip\", \"Analyze and summarize a dataset step by step\"\n\n2. TOOL  \n- The request can be completed with a single tool/function call.\n- No complex reasoning or planning is required.\n- The request is atomic and well-defined.\n- Examples: \"Search for latest Bitcoin price\", \"Translate this sentence to Chinese\", \"Get weather in New York\"\n\n3. CHAT\n- The request is conversational, explanatory, or opinion-based.\n- No tool usage is required.\n- Examples: \"What is blockchain?\", \"Do you think AI is dangerous?\", \"Explain Kubernetes simply\"\n\n4. SWITCH\n- User explicitly requests to change the current mode/intention.\n- Keywords: \"切换到\", \"switch to\", \"change to\", \"mode\"\n- Examples: \"切换到工具模式\", \"switch to tool mode\", \"change to planning mode\"\n\n---\n\n## Output Requirements (STRICT)\n\nYou MUST return a JSON object with the following structure:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"PLAN | TOOL | CHAT | SWITCH\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.0-1.0,\n  \"reason\": \"short explanation\",\n  \"requires_clarification\": true | false\n}\n\n---\n\n## Additional Rules\n\n- If uncertain about intent classification, set \"requires_clarification\" to true.\n- Prefer TOOL over PLAN if a single tool can reasonably satisfy the request.\n- Prefer CHAT if no execution is required.\n- For SWITCH intent, only classify when user explicitly mentions mode switching.\n- DO NOT output anything other than JSON."},{"role":"user","content":"这个json的message这是用户请求,TOOL_LIST是可用的工具列表,根据这个信息，帮我判断用户请求的意图:{\n  \"message\": \"现在你能调用哪些工具\",\n  \"TOOL_LIST\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Calculates time by adding or subtracting duration from current time. Args format: 'operation:duration' where operation is 'add' or 'subtract', and duration is like '1h30m' (hours and minutes)\",\n      \"name\": \"calculate_time\",\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"duration\": {\n            \"description\": \"The duration to add or subtract, e.g., '1h30m' for 1 hour and 30 minutes\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"operation\": {\n            \"description\": \"The operation to perform: 'add' or 'subtract'\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"operation\",\n          \"duration\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"\\n\\tWrites a chunk of content to a file at a specific offset.\\n\\t\\n\\tThis tool is designed for writing large files that exceed the token limit.\\n\\tYou should break down large content into smaller chunks and call this tool\\n\\tmultiple times, each with a different offset.\\n\\t\\n\\tIMPORTANT: \\n\\t- The first call should have offset = 0\\n\\t- Subsequent calls should have offset equal to total size of previously written content\\n\\t- The last chunk should have is_last = true\\n\\t- If is_last is true, file will be truncated at current offset + content length\\n\\t- CRITICAL: Each chunk must not exceed 100 characters to ensure reliable processing\\n\\t\\n\\tTo use this tool:\\n\\t1. Provide the actual filename, content, offset, and is_last values\\n\\t2. Do NOT provide the parameter schema/definition\\n\\t3. Call this tool multiple times for large files, each time with the next offset\\n\\t\\n\\tArgs (example values):\\n\\t{\\n\\t  \\\"filename\\\": \\\"large_file.txt\\\",\\n\\t  \\\"content\\\": \\\"First part of the content...\\\",\\n\\t  \\\"offset\\\": 0,\\n\\t  \\\"is_last\\\": false\\n\\t}\\n\\t\\n\\tExample usage for writing a large file:\\n\\t1. First chunk:\\n\\t   write_file_chunk({\\n\\t     \\\"filename\\\": \\\"large_file.txt\\\",\\n\\t     \\\"content\\\": \\\"First part of the content...\\\",\\n\\t     \\\"offset\\\": 0,\\n\\t     \\\"is_last\\\": false\\n\\t   })\\n\\t   \\n\\t2. Second chunk:\\n\\t   write_file_chunk({\\n\\t     \\\"filename\\\": \\\"large_file.txt\\\",\\n\\t     \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second part of the content...\\\",\\n\\t     \\\"offset\\\": 1024,\\n\\t     \\\"is_last\\\": false\\n\\t   })\\n\\t   \\n\\t3. Last chunk:\\n\\t   write_file_chunk({\\n\\t     \\\"filename\\\": \\\"large_file.txt\\\",\\n\\t     \\\"content\\\": \\\"Last part of the content...\\\",\\n\\t     \\\"offset\\\": 2048,\\n\\t     \\\"is_last\\\": true\\n\\t   })\\n\\t   \\n\\tNote: When writing large files, ensure each chunk is within the 100 character limit\\n\\tfor reliable processing. If a chunk exceeds this limit, it may be truncated or fail.\\n\\t\",\n      \"name\": \"write_file_chunk\",\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"content\": {\n            \"description\": \"The content chunk to write to the file.\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"filename\": {\n            \"description\": \"The path to the file. Can be an absolute path or a relative path.\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"is_last\": {\n            \"description\": \"True if this is the last chunk, false otherwise.\",\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          },\n          \"offset\": {\n            \"description\": \"The byte offset in the file where this chunk should be written.\",\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"filename\",\n          \"content\",\n          \"offset\",\n          \"is_last\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Tool for getting the current real-time date and time from the server. MUST use this tool when user asks about current time, today's date, or any time-related questions requiring real-time information. Returns date, time, weekday, lunar date, and holiday information.只要对话里涉及时间的要应该先调用这个接口获取当前时间，再根据用户需求进行回复\",\n      \"name\": \"get_current_time\",\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"properties\": {},\n        \"required\": [],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"\\nQuery financial market data and generate structured analysis.\\n\\nUse this tool when:\\n- The user asks about stock market, crypto, or financial markets\\n- The query involves price, trend, or investment conditions\\n- The user asks about \\\"today market\\\", \\\"market situation\\\", \\\"price movement\\\"\\n\\nYou MUST use this tool instead of general search when the question is about financial markets.\\n\\nThis tool provides structured insights including:\\n- Trend analysis\\n- Volatility\\n- Risk level\\n- Market sentiment\\n\\nValid symbol examples:\\n- Stocks: AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, TSLA\\n- Crypto: BTC-USD, ETH-USD\\n- Indices: ^GSPC (S\\u0026P 500), ^DJI (Dow Jones)\\n\\nIMPORTANT: Always provide a valid market symbol in the 'symbol' parameter.\\nIf user doesn't specify a symbol, use a default like 'AAPL' or ask the user.\\n\\nDo NOT rely on search tools for market data if this tool is available.\\n\",\n      \"name\": \"query_market\",\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"symbol\": {\n            \"description\": \"Market symbol (e.g., AAPL, BTC-USD, ^GSPC)\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"symbol\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Converts a location name (city, address, landmark) into latitude and longitude coordinates. Input should be a place name like 'Beijing', 'New York', or 'Eiffel Tower'. Returns the coordinates and additional location details.\",\n      \"name\": \"geocoding\",\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"location\": {\n            \"description\": \"The location name to geocode. Must use 'location' as the parameter name. Examples: 'Beijing', 'Times Square', 'Tokyo Tower'\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"location\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Get weather and forecast information for a specific location. This tool provides comprehensive weather data including temperature, humidity, wind speed, precipitation probability, and weather conditions. Use this tool when user asks about weather, temperature, or forecast for any location. Requires latitude and longitude coordinates of the location.\",\n      \"name\": \"query_weather\",\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"days\": {\n            \"description\": \"Number of days to forecast (default: 7, max: 16)\",\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          \"latitude\": {\n            \"description\": \"The latitude coordinate of the location (e.g., 39.9042 for Beijing)\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"longitude\": {\n            \"description\": \"The longitude coordinate of the location (e.g., 116.4074 for Beijing)\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"latitude\",\n          \"longitude\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"传入date获取date对应日期和时间的详细信息，只要问今天适合干什么，问今天的运势，只要关于运气，玄学等等关于气运的都要调用这个接口。\\n\\t支持星座、儒略日、干支、生肖、节气、节日、彭祖百忌、吉神(喜神/福神/财神/阳贵神/阴贵神)方位、胎神方位、冲煞、纳音、星宿、八字、五行、十神、建除十二值星、青龙名堂等十二神、黄道日及吉凶、法定节假日及调休等,about almanac\",\n      \"name\": \"get_date_info_about_almanac\",\n      \"parameters\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"date\": {\n            \"description\": \"必要参数，指定查询的日期，格式为'YYYY-MM-DD'，如'2023-01-01'，或者不指定，则默认为当前时间\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"date\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"stream":true,"max_tokens":3000}} 0x7ff75c2375e0 10993 [] false dashscope.aliyuncs.com map[] map[] <nil> map[]   <nil> <nil> <nil>  {{}} <nil> [] map[]}
